Upstream modifications convert premise/hypothesis pairs to typed entailment,
contradiction and neutral choices, deterministically reorder options, and preserve
source identifiers/gold/provenance with connected seed/premise grouping. Our local
preparation preserves complete state/metadata and original targets, reorders options
and targets together, isolates connected groups, selects whole-group subsets and
excludes components represented in the older incompatible extraction backend.
See docs/DATA.md and manifests/data-lineage.json for the exact chain and hashes.

The pngwn/typed-decisions-v2 and pngwn/typed-decisions-v2-system-one datasets and
HotpotQA/MMLU-Pro names in older summaries are related lineage references, not a
verified recipe for downloading these exact selected records. Their independent
terms would still apply to any separately obtained material. They must not replace
the direct Open-Jev attribution above.

## What is and is not redistributed

- Included: head weights/normalization; project code and patches; figures; aggregate
  metrics; dev predictions; ordered split membership, categories, numeric targets,
  hard-label indices, permutations and hash commitments.
- Not included: selected train/dev/test/OOD/cal state/question/option wording, full
  task metadata or conversations; backbone weights; hidden-state activation archives; omitted Wiki
  payloads; sealed benchmark items; separate private/internal control-task bodies.
- Membership identifiers are intentionally linkable to the public upstream and may
  reveal task/category names. This is an index, not a claim of anonymization.
- Included baseline prediction files contain identifiers, labels, probabilities and
  predictions rather than task-body/state text. Hashes are commitments, not a grant
  of rights or a way to recover withheld content.
- Backbone: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO and its referenced abliterated IQ3_S build are
  third-party assets, not included; redistribution rights have not been established.
- Strata is not included as a complete upstream source/runtime distribution; its
  own license governs its sources and derivative patch portions.
- JevBench public-231 task payloads and its scorer are included under the upstream
  MIT license above. This is the public 231-task snapshot, not an official sealed/full
  benchmark result or a redistribution of withheld train/dev/test split text.

